OniMeiRubbingHigekiri: {
	DisplayName: Higekiri
	Tooltip: Massively increases damage against wounded foes, personal execution refunds stance; weapon damage -2%
	Origin: The night of the Minamoto clan's test cut, this blade took the criminal's head and the beard beneath the chin in a single stroke. The name Higekiri began that night
	Power:
		'''
		"Beard-Cutter": direct blade hits deal scaling damage against targets below 35% life, scaling higher as life depletes
		Deals up to +60% damage to regular enemies, and up to +45% damage to bosses
		If the strike slays the target directly, refunds 8 stance (at most once per action)
		'''
	Burden: Weapon base damage reduced by 2%
}

OniMeiRubbingOnikiri: {
	DisplayName: Onikiri
	Tooltip: Original inscription, preserves Onikiri's baseline attributes without bonus or penalty
	Origin: Watanabe no Tsuna wielded this blade at the bridge of Ichijo-Modoribashi and severed an oni's arm, driving it away in agony. The demon-slaying blade received the inscription Onikiri, carved deep into the tang across the ages
	Power: Preserves all baseline properties of Onikiri without additional bonuses or effects
	Burden: None
}

OniMeiRubbingShishinoko: {
	DisplayName: Shishi-no-ko
	Tooltip: Completing the full five-beat combo adds crossing blade waves on the finisher; combo interval +2%
	Origin: Legend tells this blade once rested by the lord's pillow, roaring like a lion in the dead of night and shaking the estate. Astounded by its power, the master inlaid its name in gold onto the tang, renaming it Shishi-no-ko
	Power:
		'''
		"Lion's Roar": completing the full five-beat basic combo without interruption by Flash Step or arts
		The fifth beat releases two crossing slash waves, each dealing damage equal to 22% of weapon base damage
		'''
	Burden: Basic combo attack interval extended by 2%
}

OniMeiRubbingTomokiri: {
	DisplayName: Tomokiri
	Tooltip: Flash Step cancelling a combo leaves a delayed echo slash in place; damage taken +6% while held and stacks dash vigor cost
	Origin: Two treasured Minamoto blades were tested edge against edge; this blade's edge proved too sharp, cleaving its companion clean in two. Renamed Tomokiri for slaying its fellow blade, its temperament grew ever more violent
	Power:
		'''
		"Guilt Echo": using Kamui Flash Step to cancel the current combo leaves the interrupted swing behind as an echo
		After a short delay it strikes in place, dealing damage equal to 35% of weapon base damage
		'''
	Burden:
		'''
		Damage taken while holding this blade increased by 6%
		Each Guilt Echo stacks 1 layer of "Guilt" (up to 3), each layer making the next Flash Step cost 4 more vigor
		Landing a follow-up Zanshin strike after a dash clears all Guilt
		'''
}

OniMeiRubbingKazehi: {
	DisplayName: Kaze-hi
	Tooltip: Greatly reduces vigor cost of Kamui Flash Step and Sakura Flight; ink brand explosion damage -20%
	Origin: The swordsmith carved a long, straight groove into the blade to guide wind along the steel. As it swings the wind arrives first, dying down just as the edge returns to its sheath
	Power: '''"Wind-Rider": Kamui Flash Step vigor cost reduced by 15%, Sakura Flight vigor drain rate reduced by 20%'''
	Burden: Explosion damage of ink brands left by Kamui Flash Step reduced by 20%
}

OniMeiRubbingChihi: {
	DisplayName: Chi-hi
	Tooltip: Blade hits grant extra vigor; natural vigor recovery greatly slowed and recovery delay increased
	Origin: The blood groove carved into the steel is deep and resolute. The smith declared upon completion that this channel is cut for warm blood: the more it bathes in blood, the swifter the wielder's breath returns
	Power:
		'''
		"Bloodflow": the first hit of each basic combo beat restores 1 extra vigor
		Zanshin strikes following a Kamui Flash Step restore 4 extra vigor on hit
		'''
	Burden: Natural vigor recovery speed reduced by 35%, skills consuming vigor require an additional 0.3s delay before natural recovery begins
}

OniMeiRubbingFudo: {
	DisplayName: Fudo
	Tooltip: Taking hits during uninterruptible art animations consumes stance to heavily reduce damage; stance gain -15%
	Origin: The carver chiseled the seed syllable "Kan" into the steel, reverently inscribing Fudo Myoo backed by blazing flames. Taken from the Immovable One's vow: through raging storms, sitting unmoved as a mountain
	Power:
		'''
		"Immovable Guard": taking damage during the locked animations of Zanshin strike, Annihilating Flash, or Finale Slash
		Consumes 20 stance to reduce damage taken to 65% and knockback to 25% (2.5-second cooldown)
		'''
	Burden: Standard stance gain speed reduced by 15%, cannot guard against dismemberment self-damage
}

OniMeiRubbingKurikara: {
	DisplayName: Kurikara
	Tooltip: Executions grant three stacks of dragonfire, combo finisher consumes dragonfire for a coiling slash; max vigor -10%
	Origin: The blade is carved with the aspect of Kurikara the Dragon King: a black dragon coiled around a sacred sword, jaws agape to swallow the tip. Gold inlay gleams in the scales, bearing Buddhist wrath against evil
	Power:
		'''
		"Dragonfire Loop": successfully executing a foe grants 3 stacks of dragonfire lasting 10s
		Completing a full five-beat basic combo consumes 1 stack to unleash a forward coiling slash, dealing 50% of weapon base damage
		'''
	Burden: Max vigor reduced by 10%
}

OniMeiRubbingTessetsu: {
	DisplayName: Tessetsu
	Tooltip: First hit of each combo beat deals +25% damage to mechanical and metal foes; regular weapon damage -10%
	Origin: A connoisseur once sneered at this blade, mocking its hollow reputation and dull color like raw iron. The smith took no offense, chiseling the mockery straight into the tang: raw iron shows its true worth when shattering steel
	Power: '''"Iron-Cut": the first hit of each basic combo beat deals +25% damage to foes that spark upon taking damage, such as machines and metal entities'''
	Burden: Weapon base damage reduced by 10%
}

OniMeiRubbingKyushu: {
	DisplayName: Kyushu
	Tooltip: Massive execution damage scaling strictly against heads or standalone targets; regular weapon damage -3%
	Origin: In ancient times many prized blades changed their names to boast of slaying generals. This master eschewed such vanity: heads fall as before, the name stays as before; true edges need no hollow titles for reverence
	Power:
		'''
		"Head-Hunt": landing direct hits on enemy heads or non-segmented standalone targets below 35% life deals massive damage scaling with missing life
		Deals up to +85% damage to regular enemies, and up to +60% damage to bosses
		'''
	Burden: Weapon base damage reduced by 3%, ineffective against body or tail segments of enemies
}

OniMeiRubbingIkiai: {
	DisplayName: Ikiai
	Tooltip: Five-beat combo finisher fires a piercing sword beam toward the cursor; combo attack interval +4%
	Origin: Swordsmen say that during standoffs, breath locks together between duelists; whoever matches breath first strikes first. This inscription records that very discipline
	Power: '''"Breath": completing the five-beat basic combo fires a crescent sword wave toward the cursor on the fifth beat, dealing 55% of weapon base damage, piercing up to 3 enemies'''
	Burden: Basic combo attack interval extended by 4%
}

OniMeiRubbingKyoko: {
	DisplayName: Kyoko
	Tooltip: Stepping back banks force for massive melee damage, slows nearby foes when idle; rapid point-blank spam causes brief blur
	Origin: A blade tester bellowed into a desolate gorge, met with utter silence. In the empty expanse, that roaring vitality coiled and stored itself within the steel
	Power:
		'''
		"Hollow Roar": remaining outside 16 tiles of enemies for 1.5s stores force
		Your first hit within 16 tiles after storing force deals +25% damage (hits landed further away do not consume this effect)
		When no enemies are near or no hits are landed for 1.5s, slows enemies within 20 tiles for 0.4s every 1.5s
		'''
	Burden: Landing 4 point-blank hits within 0.6s causes 0.4s of blurred focus, reducing point-blank damage by 5% during the blur
}

OniMeiRubbingKarikiri: {
	DisplayName: Karikiri
	Tooltip: Flash Step leaves a decoy nullifying one hit completely; damage taken increased while decoy stands or after it breaks
	Origin: A student copied his master's footwork to perfection, yet the master only sighed that it was too alike to be real. This inscription becomes a phantom form, taking a blow in place of the true body
	Power:
		'''
		"False Body": starting a Kamui Flash Step leaves a static decoy lasting 1.5s in place
		While the decoy exists, taking damage from any enemy or projectile is completely nullified by the decoy (4-second cooldown)
		'''
	Burden:
		'''
		While the decoy stands, damage taken and dash vigor cost are both increased by 12%
		For 1s after the decoy is shattered, damage taken is increased by 18% (natural expiration incurs no penalty)
		'''
}

OniMeiRubbingMokukiri: {
	DisplayName: Mokukiri
	Tooltip: Finishing a standard dash briefly empowers the next strike; whiffing still consumes the buff
	Origin: The instant a flash step settles, heaven and earth seem to fall into quiet. Seasoned swordsmen know that when killing intent is veiled in silence, the strike lands heaviest
	Power: '''"Silent Kill": for 0.75s after completing a standard Kamui Flash Step, the next basic combo swing or Zanshin strike deals +35% damage'''
	Burden: Whiffing the empowered strike still consumes the state, and dashing again clears the bonus; free dashes from executions cannot trigger Silent Kill
}

OniMeiRubbingKumokiri: {
	DisplayName: Kumo-kiri
	Tooltip: Blade hits pin three silk anchors to close a web dealing damage and binding foes; natural recovery slowed while web is woven
	Origin: Minamoto no Raiko lay bedridden with illness when a tsuchigumo disguised as a monk crept in to bind him in silk. Raiko drew his blade, severed the threads, and tracked the blood to eradicate its nest, renaming the blade Kumokiri
	Power:
		'''
		"Ink Silk": direct blade hits pin an ink silk anchor lasting 4s (the same enemy cannot be pinned again within 0.4s, adjacent anchors require roughly 6 tiles spacing)
		Pinning 3 anchors connects a triangular ink web that snaps toward the center, dealing 90% of weapon base damage to all trapped enemies and immobilizing them for 1s
		After closing the web, 1.5s cooldown is required before pinning anchors again
		'''
	Burden: While unclosed silk anchors remain on the field, natural vigor recovery speed is reduced by 25%
	DeedHint: Slay 30 spiders, scorpions, or arachnid creatures while holding Onikiri
}

OniMeiRubbingOnimaru: {
	DisplayName: Oni-maru
	Tooltip: Standing still launches the blade to strike nearby foes; conventional blade handling disabled while detached
	Origin: Onimaru Kunitsuna, one of the Five Great Swords. Legend tells Hojo Tokimasa was haunted nightly by a demon until the blade toppled onto a brazier on its own, severing the carved demon head and banishing the evil forever
	Power:
		'''
		"Self-Cut": standing still with the blade for 1s enters standby
		Every 1.5s during standby, consumes 10 vigor to fly toward an enemy within 40 tiles, delivering a strike dealing 140% of weapon base damage before returning
		'''
	Burden: While the blade is flying, basic combos, Kamui Flash Step, and Sakura Flight cannot be used; will not launch if no valid targets are nearby
	DeedHint: Stand still while holding Onikiri, take a hit, and maintain standing still for a cumulative 10s
}

OniMeiRubbingRaikiri: {
	DisplayName: Rai-kiri
	Tooltip: Fifth beat and arts call heavenly lightning under open sky; combo interval +6%, cannot call lightning under ceilings
	Origin: Tachibana Dosetsu sheltered from rain beneath a tree when lightning struck; Dosetsu drew his blade and cleaved the lightning bolt, miraculously surviving. His sword was renamed Raikiri, renowned across all provinces
	Power:
		'''
		"Thunder-Cut": when the fifth combo beat, Zanshin strike, Annihilating Flash, or Finale Slash hits an enemy under an open sky, calls down a thunder pillar onto the target
		The lightning pillar deals 70% of weapon base damage; in thunderstorms, up to 3 lightning pillars are called down per strike
		'''
	Burden: Basic combo attack interval extended by 6% (active in clear weather too); blocked overhead or underground cannot call lightning
	DeedHint: Slay any boss while holding Onikiri under an open sky during a thunderstorm
}

OniMeiRubbingNuekiri: {
	DisplayName: Nue-kiri
	Tooltip: Completing a five-beat combo mid-air turns the finisher into a ground slam dragging foes; cannot dash briefly after landing
	Origin: Ominous clouds gathered over the palace as the beast Nue wailed in the night. Minamoto no Yorimasa drew his bow to fell the beast, drawing his blade downward in its fall to slay it, taking that very plunging force
	Power:
		'''
		"Nue-Dive": completing the basic combo at least 3 tiles off the ground turns the fifth beat into a powerful groundward dive
		The impact generates a shockwave roughly 12 tiles in radius, dealing 120% of weapon base damage and dragging nearby foes toward the impact
		'''
	Burden: Cannot use Kamui Flash Step for about 0.7s after landing; ground swings retain the standard horizontal fifth beat
	DeedHint: At night and over 30 tiles above ground, slay a flying enemy while holding Onikiri
}

OniMeiRubbingKamihi: {
	DisplayName: Kami-hi
	Tooltip: Dashing through enemies leaves paper effigies; striking effigies transmits damage and vulnerability; dash cost +12% while paper stands
	Origin: A master paper-mounter cuts with divine precision, separating form from shadow in one stroke. This groove learns the art of peeling form, shearing the enemy's shadow into Omote to cut paper as flesh
	Power:
		'''
		"Paper-Effigy": Kamui Flash Step passing through an enemy leaves an effigy lasting 7s at the landing point (up to 2 effigies simultaneously)
		Attacking the effigy deals 80% of weapon base damage, transmitting the full damage directly to the true body
		Inflicts a 1.5s wounded state on the true body, during which it takes 12% increased damage from Onikiri
		'''
	Burden: While paper effigies exist on the field, Kamui Flash Step vigor cost is increased by 12%
	DeedHint: In Ura, sever 20 omokage paper effigies while holding Onikiri
}

OniMeiRubbingSorahi: {
	DisplayName: Sora-hi
	Tooltip: Natural recovery doubled and grants an extra air dash while airborne; recovery pauses briefly upon landing
	Origin: The smith kept an eccentric theory: human vigor turns sluggish the moment feet touch the earth. Only by crafting the blade featherlight to leap through the air can one align with heaven's wind and draw vitality
	Power:
		'''
		"Air-Groove": natural vigor recovery speed is doubled while airborne, granting one additional air dash
		Completing an air dash leaves you hovering at the endpoint for 0.5s
		'''
	Burden: Natural vigor recovery pauses entirely for 0.75s after landing; ground Flash Step vigor cost increased by 10%
	DeedHint: Remain airborne continuously for 15s, landing at least 5 hits with Onikiri during the flight
}

OniMeiRubbingKagamihi: {
	DisplayName: Kagami-hi
	Tooltip: Flash Step endpoint erects a paper mirror replica copying your next strike; weapon base damage -5%
	Origin: Mirror polishers know the reflection seems synchronized yet carries a faint delay. The groove carver seized that very delay, letting the mirror phantom swing a fraction behind
	Power:
		'''
		"Mirror Echo": Kamui Flash Step endpoint erects a paper mirror phantom lasting 2s
		When you swing your next blade strike, the phantom synchronously copies the cut and shatters, dealing 45% of weapon base damage
		'''
	Burden: Weapon base damage reduced by 5%; the replicated strike swings from the mirror's position and orientation, dependent on placement
	DeedHint: Slay a Mimic using the Zanshin strike (Calamity Clone's counterfeit chests also count)
}

OniMeiRubbingAmahi: {
	DisplayName: Ama-hi
	Tooltip: Sakura Flight drops ink rain that pools into binding mire; Sakura Flight vigor cost +15%
	Origin: Gutters catching rain beneath eaves share this name. The smith fashioned the groove after roof channels: caught rain must not fall in vain, dripping down upon the foes waiting beneath the blade
	Power:
		'''
		"Ink Rain": cruising in Sakura Flight drops an ink bead dealing 12% of weapon base damage every 0.1s
		Ink beads spread into puddles upon landing, immobilizing enemies entering the mire for 0.5s
		'''
	Burden: Sakura Flight vigor drain rate increased by 15%
	DeedHint: Cruise continuously in Sakura Flight during rain for 10s
}

OniMeiRubbingTsuzurihi: {
	DisplayName: Tsuzuri-hi
	Tooltip: Ink brands from a single dash detonate and connect lines; single ink brand base damage -30%
	Origin: Bookbinders stitch loose leaves with needle and thread, pulling tight to bind loose sheets into a volume. This groove treats ink brands as stitches, closing the circle into a killing array
	Power: '''"Mark-Stitch": multiple ink brands left from a single Kamui Flash Step detonate together, forming intersecting cutting lines between one another, each dealing 35% of weapon base damage'''
	Burden: Single ink brand base damage reduced by 30% (if a dash passes through only one target, overall damage is reduced)
	DeedHint: Pass through at least 6 distinct enemies in a single Kamui Flash Step
}

OniMeiRubbingBonsho: {
	DisplayName: Bonsho
	Tooltip: Full stance without releasing executions automatically tolls the bell; costs half stance to replace the execution
	Origin: Temple bells require a striker to ring, yet the ancient bell carved on this steel waits for no external hand. Building full momentum without release causes the bell to toll of itself, sounding alarm across the wild
	Power:
		'''
		"Bell-Toll": remaining at full stance for 3s without releasing Finale Slash causes the blade to toll on its own
		Releases a shockwave dealing 60% of weapon base damage to all enemies within 30 tiles and immobilizing them for 1.5s, dropping stance to 50
		'''
	Burden: The toll directly consumes full stance and forfeits the current Finale Slash opportunity
	DeedHint: Slay any boss throughout the entire battle without ever using Annihilating Flash or Finale Slash
}

OniMeiRubbingHannya: {
	DisplayName: Hannya
	Tooltip: Low life manifests the demon face for extra damage and lifesteal; damage taken increased during demon face, normal damage -4%
	Origin: The Noh Hannya mask captures the moment a woman's grief turns human features into a demon. Carved on the blade, it signifies that when cornered at death's door, one's nature inverts into an asura of wrath
	Power:
		'''
		"Mask-Shift": dropping below 35% life manifests the furious demon mask: blade damage +20%, each hit restores 0.5% max life
		Landing 3 hits during the demon mask manifests a ghost face that bites the target for 50% of weapon base damage
		'''
	Burden: Damage taken increased by 15% during demon mask; while above 35% life in normal form, weapon base damage is reduced by 4%
	DeedHint: Slay any boss while holding Onikiri with your own life sitting below 10%
}

OniMeiRubbingKaresansui: {
	DisplayName: Karesansui
	Tooltip: Standing still rakes a persistent sand garden that cuts foes and speeds stance gain; moving cancels charge
	Origin: Garden masters rake boundless waves from fine sand without water. The carver channeled that spirit into the blade: only those who stand in calm concentration can furrow a garden of stillness with sword-intent
	Power:
		'''
		"Sand Garden": standing still for 1.5s rakes a sand garden field 20 tiles in radius lasting 5s
		Deals 18% of weapon base damage to enemies inside every 0.5s
		Standing within your own sand garden increases stance gain speed by 30%
		'''
	Burden: Opening the garden requires remaining still to charge, moving cancels the charge progress
	DeedHint: Fight continuously for 30s while holding Onikiri without moving or taking any damage
}

OniMeiRubbingSenju: {
	DisplayName: Senju
	Tooltip: Finale Slash freeze adds six ghost arms striking together; resets vigor to zero and locks dashing for 3s
	Origin: The Thousand-Armed Kannon extends boundless hands to ferry mortal suffering. The carver inlaid this aspect into the steel, establishing this rule: every soul ferried by the art must be met with a blade in hand
	Power: '''"Thousand Arms": during the Finale Slash freeze, six sword-bearing ghost arms rise behind you to strike together, each dealing 30% of weapon base damage'''
	Burden: Executing Finale Slash resets vigor to zero, and Kamui Flash Step cannot be used for 3s
	DeedHint: Slay 8 distinct bosses using Finale Slash while holding Onikiri
}

OniMeiRubbingKogehi: {
	DisplayName: Koge-hi
	Tooltip: Kamui Flash Step leaves scorching ground along its path; weapon base damage -4%
	Origin: The smith dwelt beside lava shallows, watching those who failed to mind their footing. He opened this fire groove to leap clear, leaving the searing heat behind for pursuers
	Power:
		'''
		"Scorch Trail": Kamui Flash Step leaves up to 5 scorching zones lasting 1.5s along its path
		Enemies stepping into scorched ground take continuous burn damage equal to 14% of weapon base damage every 0.5s
		New burns overlapping within 2 tiles of older ones simply refresh the duration
		'''
	Burden: Weapon base damage reduced by 4%, lost output must be recouped through scorch trails
}

OniMeiRubbingKanhi: {
	DisplayName: Kan-hi
	Tooltip: Disengaging from combat greatly accelerates natural vigor recovery; Flash Step and Sakura Flight costs +8%
	Origin: A long bench rests before the sword shop where the smith watches the busy market when resting. In stillness breath is nourished, and this groove captures that tranquil rest
	Power: '''"Quiet Breath": after disengaging from combat and landing no hits for 2s, natural vigor recovery speed increases to 2.25x'''
	Burden: Kamui Flash Step and Sakura Flight vigor costs both increase by 8%
}

OniMeiRubbingTodohi: {
	DisplayName: Todo-hi
	Tooltip: Blade hits bind and slow enemies; Flash Step start has a brief startup delay
	Origin: A peculiar quench left the edge dragging through flesh, hindering whatever it cuts. The smith took pride in it: what is bound is the struck foe, not the hand wielding the steel
	Power: '''"Ink-Bound": direct blade hits slow enemy movement for 0.6s, dropping regular enemies to 88% and bosses to 96%'''
	Burden: Kamui Flash Step has an additional 0.1s startup delay; Ink-Bound and Numbed do not stack on the same enemy, only applying the strongest slow
}

OniMeiRubbingShiorihi: {
	DisplayName: Shiori-hi
	Tooltip: Slaying a foe launches a pruning blade at nearby wounded enemies; natural recovery -10%, whiffed Zanshin penalizes vigor
	Origin: Gardeners prune foliage with care: wherever the shears move, withered stems nearby are clipped in the same pass. The one who opened this groove followed that craft
	Power:
		'''
		"Petal-Prune": directly slaying a target searches within 15 tiles for another enemy below 50% life
		Launches a pruning blade to pursue that target, dealing 25% of weapon base damage (no cooldown if no target is found; 0.75s cooldown on trigger)
		'''
	Burden:
		'''
		Natural vigor recovery speed reduced by 10%
		Zanshin strike following a dash consumes 2 extra vigor if it whiffs
		Kills caused by the pruning blade cannot chain into another prune
		'''
}

OniMeiRubbingShiohi: {
	DisplayName: Shio-hi
	Tooltip: Swinging to the tidal rhythm restores vigor on hit, on-tide Zanshin strikes harder; off-beat combos slightly weakened
	Origin: The smith grew up by the sea, grinding blades to the rhythm of swelling tides. Tides rise and fall as human breath ebbs and flows; striking on the surge, the sea returns vigor
	Power:
		'''
		"Tide-Beat": a tide marker pulses on a 0.8s cycle below the vigor bar, the 0.2s peak being the on-tide window
		Basic combos swung within the on-tide window restore 3 extra vigor on first hit; on-tide Zanshin strikes deal +8% damage
		'''
	Burden: Basic combos swung off-beat deal 3% reduced damage (judged at the moment the swing key is pressed, not on hit)
}

OniMeiRubbingShibori: {
	DisplayName: Shibori
	Tooltip: Dashing through or taking hits during art animations numbs foes; standard stance gain -15%
	Origin: Novice swordsmen must endure the ache of numbed wrists. The carver turned the principle around: if I endure one measure of shock, the striking foe shall suffer ten
	Power:
		'''
		"Numb-Counter": Kamui Flash Step passing through an enemy inflicts the "Numbed" state directly
		Taking contact damage during locked art animations consumes 15 stance to reduce damage to 85% and numb the attacker (1.5s cooldown)
		Numbed enemies move slower for 0.75s (regular foes down to 90%, bosses to 98%) and deal 10% reduced contact damage
		'''
	Burden: Standard stance gain speed reduced by 15%
}

OniMeiRubbingChinmei: {
	DisplayName: Chinmei
	Tooltip: Heavily reduces hostile projectile damage and knockback; standard stance gain -15%
	Origin: Arrows and stones clash before the battle lines, panicking the weak. The veteran who carved this line knew that amid flying arrows, planting one's stance firm cuts the wound in half
	Power: '''"Quell": taking damage from hostile projectiles reduces damage by 12% and reduces knockback taken to 35%'''
	Burden: Standard stance gain speed reduced by 15%; this carving offers limited benefit in pure close-quarters melee combat
}

OniMeiRubbingAshidome: {
	DisplayName: Ashidome
	Tooltip: Standing still stores force to heavily boost the next fifth beat or art; moving clears charge
	Origin: A master's first lesson: unsteady footing wastes all craft. Only with firm roots can vigor gather, and gathered vigor unleashed shatters mountains
	Power: '''"Planted-Step": standing still for 0.75s stores force, increasing the damage of the next basic combo fifth beat, Zanshin strike, Annihilating Flash, or Finale Slash by 25%'''
	Burden: The empowered strike is consumed upon attack, whiffing does not refund; moving immediately clears all stored force
}

OniMeiRubbingYoen: {
	DisplayName: Yoen
	Tooltip: Executions leave persistent burning embers at the impact; max vigor -5%, dash cost +10% while embers burn
	Origin: After the forge fire is banked, embers within the hearth retain warmth throughout the night. The smith borrowed this nature: though flames recede, the searing heat remains
	Power:
		'''
		"Ember-Field": successfully executing a foe leaves an ember field lasting 3s at the impact
		Enemies within the field take burn damage equal to 16% of weapon base damage every 0.75s
		Only one field can exist at a time; executing again moves the field to the new position
		'''
	Burden: Max vigor reduced by 5%; while the ember field burns, Kamui Flash Step vigor cost is increased by 10%
}
